4. Detailed Survey on One Use Case: Healthcare
The healthcare industry suffers from fragmented patient records, data breaches, and inefficient third-party intermediaries. Implementing blockchain solves these issues directly:

Immutable Patient Records: A patient's medical history can be stored on a blockchain ledger. Because the ledger is immutable, hackers cannot tamper with or delete critical health data.   
Lab practice - III Lab Manual.pdf

Interoperability and Sharing: Patients can grant specific doctors or hospitals access to their decentralized records instantly using cryptographic keys, eliminating the need to manually transfer files between different hospital systems.

Cost and Time Efficiency: By removing third-party verification and intermediaries from medical billing and insurance claims, settlements are processed faster and administrative costs are drastically reduced.   
Lab practice - III Lab Manual.pdf

Drug Traceability: Blockchain can trace pharmaceuticals from the manufacturer to the patient, ensuring tighter security and preventing counterfeit drugs from entering the supply chain.   
